SCENARIO-You are a junior developer at a fintech startup building a digital wallet app. The team is
         debating between Waterfall and Agile methodology. The project has frequently
        changing requirements and the client expects to review working features every two weeks.
Recommendation:  
  Agile methodology.

Justification: 
  Agile operates in short, iterative cycles (sprints), making it ideal for client reviews every two weeks and rapidly changing requirements.

Risks of Waterfall:
  Inflexible Scope: Rigid upfront planning makes incorporating changing requirements late in development costly and difficult.
  Delayed Feedback: Working software is delivered only near the end, delaying client reviews and increasing the risk of delivering an unwanted product.  
